2026-09-29T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-2288) 'guest capabilities: macaroons minted from ReBAC
 # uuid: b104527a-e1b3-57f6-985b-477c3776a6d9
 # tags: rfd:title, rfd:flight-level:l1
 RFD:Discussion  1 RFD
 Serials:VSekaiFabric

2026-09-29T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2288) 'A guest ELF reaches outside its own memory only through a capability: a macaroon that a ReBAC check mints, checked once at the host call and cached for the VM
 # tags: rfd:feature, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2288  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-29T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2288) 'the godot-sandbox addon's host-call table, every guest ELF that makes host calls, and the ReBAC tuples of RFD66606-2200
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2288  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-29T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2288) 'Does a guest ELF reach outside its own memory only through a macaroon minted from ReBAC?
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2288  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-29T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2288) 'A ReBAC check on every host call is too slow for calls made every frame, and no check makes every guest a leak.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2288  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-29T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2288) 'Read RFD66606-2200 next for the ReBAC tuples that decide what a capability grants.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2288  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-29T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2288) 'guest capabilities: macaroons minted from ReBAC
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2288  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-29T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2288) 'Capabilities are an allowlist. A guest starts with none. Each host call that reaches outside the guest's own memory needs one, and a new need gets a new, narrow capability, never a wider old one. A capability is a macaroon. A ReBAC check (RFD66606-2200) mints it, with caveats that name the VM, the verb, the object, an expiry at most 5 s away and the VM's revocation epoch. The host verifies the macaroon's HMAC chain once and caches the grant in that VM's host-call table, so each later call costs a bit test and two integer compares. The host verifies the macaroon again every 5 s. Bumping a VM's epoch voids its cached grants at their next call. A guest's writes to its own memory are not host calls, and nothing checks them.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2288  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-29T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2288) '- RFD66606-2200, the ReBAC tuples that decide what a capability grants.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2288  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-29T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2288) 'Related
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2288  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-29T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2288) 'RFD66606-2287, whose CA relies on no transfer capability for its VM. Gate, unmet: no macaroon minting, grant table or epoch code exists in any product repo (searched 2026-11-11), so the acceptance is not met.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2288  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-29T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2288) 'Why check once per grant
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2288  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-29T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2288) 'RFD66606-2287's CA keeps its root key in guest memory, but a VM transfer carries all of that memory, and so does a host read of it. So the check runs once per grant, needs no network round trip, and costs little to repeat.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2288  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-29T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2288) 'The macaroon
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2288  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-29T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2288) 'The host that runs the guest holds the macaroon root key and mints. Before it mints, it asks the ReBAC store whether a tuple relates the subject to the object with the verb. No tuple, no macaroon. The caveats are `vm`, `verb`, `object`, `expires` and `epoch`. A zone that hands work to another zone adds caveats before it passes the macaroon on, which narrows it without a round trip. Nobody can remove a caveat, because the HMAC chain then fails.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2288  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-29T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2288) 'The hot path
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2288  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-29T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2288) 'The host-call table holds, per VM, one bit per granted capability, its expiry and the epoch it was granted at. A host call checks the bit, compares the clock with the expiry, and compares the stored epoch with the VM's current one. Past the expiry the host verifies the macaroon again and refreshes the entry. The 5 s bound keeps a revoked grant short-lived and a retry cheap.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2288  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-29T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2288) 'Adding a capability
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2288  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-29T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2288) 'A capability names one verb on one object, and the table below carries the three that exist as `capability` declarations (RFD66606-2291, ReBAC as a DSL feature), so a reader counts them rather than reading for them. A new need adds a declaration for that narrow verb and object, and a tuple that mints it. A wider capability is not allowed; a second, narrow one is. `ca.elf` gets no `transfer` or memory-read capability.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2288  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-29T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2288) 'Checks
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2288  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-29T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2288) 'Each has a control, and each runs with the guest's real host calls.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2288  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-29T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2288) '- A host call with no capability is refused. Control: the same call with its capability goes ahead.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2288  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-29T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2288) '- A call after an epoch bump is refused; the same call before the bump goes ahead.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2288  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-29T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2288) '- A call past the expiry is refused until the macaroon verifies again.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2288  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-29T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2288) '- A macaroon with one caveat changed fails its HMAC check, and so does one with a caveat removed.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2288  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-29T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2288) '- A narrowed macaroon passed to another zone cannot do what the wider one could.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2288  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-29T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2288) '- The cost per call is measured against the same call with no check. The guest's own memory writes show no change.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2288  1 LINE
 Text:Written

